// endpoint_get_peer_delivery.proto — GetPeerDelivery: WHICH SESSIONS are the two
// ends of one cross-session message, by the vendor's delivery id for it.
//
// WHY ANYONE ASKS. A cross-session message names neither end as one of the
// host's sessions: the sender's record names the recipient only as the address
// the caller wrote, and the recipient's record names the sender only by the
// name it asserted. The one value both records share is the delivery id the
// sending vendor minted (conversation.v1.PeerDeliveryId): the sender's
// SendMessage result carries it (AgentSendMessagePeerSession.delivery_id), and
// so does the recipient's record of the message
// (PeerMessageInterSession.delivery_id). The daemon draws each end's row and
// names the session at the other end by this join.
//
// WHY THE STORE CAN ANSWER. Every session on the host writes into this one
// store, so both records are here whichever sessions hold them, each indexed by
// its delivery id at write time.
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT SCOPED TO THE CALLER'S LINEAGE, unlike GetLiveWork and
// GetAgentByVendorTask: the question is which OTHER session holds a record, so
// a lineage scope would refuse every answer the endpoint exists to give. The
// answer is agent ids, never either record's content.

